description:
Most likely the same hawk I posted previously, January 22nd. Very confident is sharp-shinned but looking for confirmation. 
Reasons I believe is sharp-shinned;
Dark back of neck, skinny legs, wide chest, tail appears to have sharp corners, looks slightly larger than mourning dove.

- all black, glossy;
- fairly large, with a straight bill;
- a very distinctive cawing call;
- fly all over, very visible and vocal at Carkeek park.
